  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 213 PM EDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nA mid level ridge centered over central CONUS will slowly shift \neastward  over the next few days. With our area along its eastern \nperiphery, northerly flow will persist across the region heading \ninto the start of the week. Combined with a weak low pressure \nfeature off the Carolina Coast, this will support a continuation of \nthe  high pressure wedge pattern seen over the last several days, \nalong with a relatively dry northeast wind component. With this in \nmind, expect mostly sunny skies and seasonable temperatures to \ncontinue through the week. Overnight lows will range from the 40s to \nlow 50s, with afternoon highs in the 70s and no chance of rain to \nround out October. \n\nAs we move into the latter half of next week, the upper level \npattern begins to shift. A developing trough across the Plains and \nits associated surface low could eventually increase our local rain \nchances as the system propagates eastward, though the outcome \nremains uncertain as we head into early November.",
